Subject: Tail calls on the record path

What this does
  Tail calls on the record path.

Why we need it
  Each was a nested `JS_CallInternal` that could not return through.

What it adds
  Record-eligible callee entered as a sibling record (old frame released, caller/ret_dst/ret_ip inherited, args/receiver/callee duplicated first); natives, bound/proxy, generator frames and entry-record calls fall back; `REGVM_TAIL_CHAIN_MAX` cap on `JSRuntime`; separate `regvm_record_fill_tail`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
