 /*
- * `return f(...)`: the callee's value leaves this frame exactly as `return`
- * does, so the handler ends in the same exit. A generator frame is handed back
- * to the monolith, whose suspension needs the interpreter's own state (see the
- * note on `regvm_t_return`).
+ * `return f(...)`: the callee's value leaves this frame as `return` does. A
+ * generator frame is handed back to the monolith.
+ *
+ * When the record path can run the callee, it enters as a sibling record: this
+ * frame is released first and the callee names this frame's caller, so a
+ * tail-recursive loop grows neither the C stack nor the arena. Everything the
+ * callee reads from this frame (the arguments, a method's receiver, the callee
+ * object) is copied before the release. Other callees take
+ * `regvm_t_tail_call_slow`.
